    {
      "name": "Azure block-blob PUT with EXPIRED sig -> 403 with a reason OUTSIDE legacy's token-expiry set (recoverable, but legacy reason-gate won't refresh)",
      "metadata": {
        "doc": [
          "Azure SAS-expiry 403 whose reason phrase is outside the legacy Python token-expiry set. SYNTHETIC / HAND-AUTHORED reason phrase — NOT captured from real Azure traffic.",
          "statusMessage 'Signature fields not well formed.' is deliberately chosen to sit OUTSIDE legacy Python's",
          "TOKEN_EXPIRATION_ERR_MESSAGE set ('Signature not valid in the specified time frame', 'Server failed to",
          "authenticate the request.'), so the reason-gate does not refresh while UD's any-403 trigger does.",
          "CAVEAT: the captured REAL Azure SAS-expiry reason is 'Server failed to authenticate the request.', which DOES",
          "match Python's gate. The genuine real-world divergence is HTTP/2 (RFC 9113 has no reason phrase, so Python's",
          "substring match never fires) — which wiremock cannot emit over HTTP/1.1. This fixture therefore demonstrates",
          "the TRIGGER mechanism (reason-gated vs any-403) with a synthetic reason; the HTTP/2 manifestation is NEEDS-RUN."
        ]
      },
      "priority": 3,
      "request": {
        "urlPathPattern": "/test-container/prefix/.*",
        "method": "PUT",
        "queryParameters": { "sig": { "equalTo": "expiredsig" } }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 403,
        "statusMessage": "Signature fields not well formed.",
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/xml",
          "x-ms-request-id": "mock-403-request-id",
          "x-ms-version": "2021-04-10",
          "x-ms-error-code": "AuthenticationFailed"
        },
        "body": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?><Error><Code>AuthenticationFailed</Code><Message>Signature fields not well formed.</Message></Error>"
      }
    },
